<title>SOUTH AFRICA: S.African money shortage rises to 9.969 bln rand.</title>
<headline>S.African money shortage rises to 9.969 bln rand.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-12-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Africa's money market shortage rose to 9.969 billion rand on Saturday from 9.703 billion rand on Friday, the Reserve Bank said on Monday.</p>
<p>Major banks on Monday quoted three-month NCD rates unchanged at between 17.40 and 17.75 percent while the 90-day BA rate was also steady at 16.70 to 17.00 percent.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
